SUMMARY:Deadline: International Vouchers
DESCRIPTION:Travel voucher for Dutch-based professionals in design\, archit
 ecture and/or digital culture who have been invited by a foreign party to 
 give a presentation\, lecture or workshop. To apply you must have submitte
 d an application to the Fund in the past five years that was positively as
 sessed (previous International Vouchers do not count).\n\nOrganisation: St
 imuleringsfonds Creatieve Industrie (Creative Industries Fund NL)\nLocatio
 n: Netherlands (for international travel)\nAward: Up to €1\,500 within E
 urope (zone 1) / up to €2\,500 outside Europe (zone 2)\nDuration: Per tr
 ip\n\nMore: https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/international-vouch
 ers?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/international-vouchers?utm_s
 ource=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands (for international travel)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stroom-den-haag-pro-research-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261105T181829Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261025
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261026
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stroom Den Haag: PRO Research
DESCRIPTION:Stroom Den Haag's PRO Research scheme contributes to the costs 
 of a research project or artist-in-residency that feeds the development of
  new work and benefits The Hague's art climate.\n\nOrganisation: Stroom De
 n Haag\nLocation: The Hague\, Netherlands. Open to Hague artists registere
 d with Stroom and to curators\, mediators\, critics\, publicists and other
 s professionally active in the contemporary art world\; applicants from ou
 tside The Hague apply with a CV.\nAward: Maximum EUR 5\,000 per research p
 roject\, up to EUR 20\,000 per applicant per calendar year. Amounts exclud
 e VAT and grants are only awarded on demonstrable financial need. No appli
 cation fee.\nDuration: Project-based\; the grant remains valid for up to t
 wo years after the decision meeting\, with 80 percent paid upfront and 20 
 percent on the final report\n\nMore: https://www.stroom.nl/en/stroom-for-a
 rtists/financial-support/pro-research?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdes
 k&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stroom.nl/en/stroom-for-artists/financial-support/pro-resea
 rch?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:The Hague\, Netherlands. Open to Hague artists registered with Str
 oom and to curators\, mediators\, critics\, publicists and others professi
 onally active in the contemporary art world\; applicants from outside The 
 Hague apply with a CV.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jan-van-eyck-residency-2028@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261105T181829Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART:20261201T222900Z
DTEND:20261201T225900Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 23:59 CET: Jan van Eyck Academie Residency 2028 (Maastrich
 t\, 11 months)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 01 Dec 2026 at 23:59 CET.\n\nThe Jan van Eyck Academie's
  general open call for its 2028 residency year: 30 to 32 artists\, curator
 s\, designers\, writers\, architects and other artistic researchers spend 
 11 months (15 January to 15 December 2028) in Maastricht\, across material
 -based and research-driven practices\, with access to the academy's labs a
 nd community.\n\nOrganisation: Jan van Eyck Academie\nLocation: Maastricht
 \, Netherlands. Open worldwide\; participants must settle in Maastricht an
 d register with the municipality (the academy applies for visas where rele
 vant).\nAward: Monthly stipend of EUR 1\,500 (EUR 2\,000 for participants 
 with children\; EUR 1\,500 per duo member or EUR 2\,500 combined for life 
 partners\; collectives up to EUR 4\,500 combined\, max three stipends)\, w
 ith rent including service costs deducted from the stipend. Plus a EUR 2\,
 000 annual working budget and a newly built\, furnished private studio apa
 rtment. Application fee EUR 65 excl. VAT (EUR 78.65 incl. VAT)\, waived fo
 r applicants from and living in OECD DAC-list countries\; enrolment fee fo
 r accepted participants EUR 2\,750 excl. VAT.\nDuration: 11 months\, 15 Ja
 nuary to 15 December 2028\; 30 to 32 positions\; selection outcome mid-May
  2027.\n\nMore: https://www.janvaneyck.nl/calendar/apply-now-jve-residency
 -2028?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.janvaneyck.nl/calendar/apply-now-jve-residency-2028?utm_sou
 rce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Maastricht\, Netherlands. Open worldwide\; participants must settl
 e in Maastricht and register with the municipality (the academy applies fo
 r visas where relevant).
END:VEVENT
